      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to the ideal equation,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math></p><p>In the given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>&#8208;</mo><mi>T</mi></math>&nbsp;diagram,</p><p>In process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>y</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mi>T</mi></math>.&nbsp;So, the process is isobaric process.</p><p>In process&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>z</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;constant. So, the process is an&nbsp;isochoric process.</p><p>In process&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>x</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;constant. So, the process is an isothermal process.</p><p>Analyzing using the ideal gas equation in each process, the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8208;</mo><mi>V</mi></math>&nbsp;graph can be drawn as shown below,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\ot1_0137_92b68ff5ff76.png\" style=\"width: 195px; height: 182px;\" /></p>"
  }
}